CHAPTER IV

DUTIES AND OBLIGATIONS OF THE REGIONAL GOVERNMENT

Article 5

1. The Regional Government has the duty to undertake prevention, handling and recovery efforts for victims of violence against Women and Children, by:a. collecting data and information about Women and Children Victims of Violence;
b. disseminating laws and regulations related to the protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence;
c. conducting education on anti-violence values against children and women; andd. conducting monitoring and evaluation of the implementation of protection of Women and Children victims of violence.
2. The Regional Government is obliged to undertake prevention, handling and recovery efforts for victims of violence against Women and Children, providing and organizing services for victims in the form of:a. providing and facilitating the establishment of integrated services for victims by involving community institutions and elements;
b. encouraging public awareness about the importance of protection for victims; andc. empowering communities for the prevention of acts of violence.

CHAPTER VI

INSTITUTION ORGANIZING PROTECTION FOR VICTIMS

Article 8

1. The Regional Government establishes an Integrated Service Center (PPT) as the Organizing, Prevention and Protection Institution for Women and Children Victims of Violence.
2. The PPT as referred to in paragraph (1) consists of elements of:a. health;
b. law enforcement;
c. social and empowerment;
d. education and religion;
e. Non-Governmental Organizations; andf. private sector.
3. Further provisions regarding the PPT as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be regulated by Regent Regulation.

